CCAAVVEEAATTSS
       AAmmqq uses a Sun registered RPC program number (300019 decimal) which may
       not be in the /etc/rpc database.

       If the TCP wrappers  library  is  available,  and  the  uussee__ttccppwwrraappppeerrss
       global aammdd..ccoonnff option is set to ‘‘yes’’, then aammdd will verify that the
       host  running  aammqq is authorized to connect.  The _a_m_d service name must
       used in the //eettcc//hhoossttss..aallllooww and //eettcc//hhoossttss..ddeennyy files.   For  example,
       to   allow  only  localhost  to  connect  to  aammdd,,  add  this  line  to
       //eettcc//hhoossttss..aallllooww::

              amd: localhost

       and this line to //eettcc//hhoossttss..ddeennyy::

              amd: ALL


